    "title": "North Fort Myers football coach Ira Riggins Jr. suspended by school district after arrest - NewsBreak",
    "text": "The North Fort Myers High School football team is beginning its preparations for the 2025 season without its head football coach. The Lee County School District suspended Red Knights first-year coach Ira Riggins Jr. pending the outcome of an investigation after he was arrested by Cape Coral police for misdemeanor battery on July 26, 2025. According to the police report, Riggins was involved in a verbal and physical altercation with his live-in girlfriend following an argument about her alleged infidelity. The News-Press does not identify victims of domestic violence. Riggins told the responding officer that a male called him from his girlfriend’s phone when she was at a bar drinking with friends. Riggins said he became angry and told his girlfriend to pack up and leave. SWFL Coaching Carousel: See who's in, who's out heading into the 2025 football season When the girlfriend arrived home, Riggins said she punched him in the face and that he pushed her to the ground in self-defense. The girlfriend told police when she arrived home, Riggins began yelling at her, took her phone away, and then pushed her onto a bed and then onto the ground. The girlfriend admitted to punching Riggins throughout the process of him pushing her. The report states officers observed some redness on the girlfriend’s shoulder and chest and a marking on her neck in the outline of a necklace. The officers observed no injuries on Riggins, who was subsequently placed under arrest. According to records, Riggins has a court appearance on Aug. 19, 2025. North Fort Myers assistant principal and former head coach Dwayne Mack will serve as the Red Knights' interim head football coach, according to a district spokesperson. Riggins and North Fort Myers athletic director Joe Bowen did not immediately return calls seeking comment. North Fort Myers announced Riggins as the football program's 14th head football on June 3, 2025. The 38-year-old former defensive coordinator replaced David Pasquale, who stepped down in May following spring football after two seasons running the program. This article originally appeared on Fort Myers News-Press: North Fort Myers football coach Ira Riggins Jr. suspended by school district after arrest",
